// Copy to Config/Secrets.xcconfig (git ignores it) and fill in Omnia's own
// app credentials. Never commit the filled-in file.
//
// Trakt:   https://app.trakt.tv/settings/apps — Production app with an
//          https redirect URI such as https://watchomnia.com/trakt (nothing
//          needs to be hosted there: Omnia signs in with a device code, and
//          Trakt only asks for the same URI again when refreshing tokens).
//          Client ID, and that redirect URI. New Trakt apps have no Client
//          Secret (PKCE); set OMNIA_TRAKT_CLIENT_SECRET only for an older app
//          that was issued one, otherwise leave it empty.
// Simkl:   https://simkl.com/settings/developer — an AUTH V2 app of type
//          "Mobile, desktop & browser apps" (no secret). Its required redirect
//          URI can be omnia://auth/simkl; Omnia signs in with Simkl's device
//          code (simkl.com/pin), which every app type may use. Client ID.
// MDBList: https://mdblist.com — OAuth client with device authorization.
//          Client ID.
// AniList: https://anilist.co/settings/developer — redirect URL
//          omnia://anilist. Client ID (a number).
//
// Values are plain text after `=`, with no quotes. xcconfig treats `//` as
// a comment, so write the Trakt redirect URI with `$()` between the
// slashes, for example: https:/$()/watchomnia.com/trakt
// (the same https redirect URI the Trakt app was created with).

OMNIA_TRAKT_CLIENT_ID =
OMNIA_TRAKT_CLIENT_SECRET =
OMNIA_TRAKT_REDIRECT_URI =
OMNIA_SIMKL_CLIENT_ID =
OMNIA_MDBLIST_CLIENT_ID =
OMNIA_ANILIST_CLIENT_ID =
